x86_64-linux  Two differences, both recorded elsewhere in this tree. `abort` is the one this case is about: cxx1 calls it where clang calls the terminate guard this suite excludes by name, exactly as noexcept-terminates.nonames records. `_ZN1RC1Ei` and `_ZN1RD1Ev` are the older trap - clang emits only the C2 and D2 forms of a constructor and destructor defined inside their class on this target, where cxx1 emits C1 and D1 as well; move-constructor.nonames and implicit-move.nonames record the same thing, and the two forms are identical for a class with no virtual base.
arm64-darwin  Only the `_abort`, this target emitting both constructor forms whatever the definition's place. Every other name agrees.
